{
  "_help": [
    "Keyframes are OFFSETS in degrees from the home pose. Joints not listed are 0 (home).",
    "Direction convention (fix mirrored servos with 'invert' in settings, never here):",
    "  HIP +   = leg swings forward      KNEE + = knee bends, foot lifts",
    "  ANKLE + = body rolls to the robot's RIGHT (weight onto the right foot); both ankles use the same sign",
    "  HEAD +  = head turns to the robot's LEFT     ARM + = arm raises forward/up",
    "Gaits loop forever while the joystick is held. Each frame takes motion.step_ms (scaled by speed).",
    "Gestures play once; each frame has its own 'ms'. 'hold': true keeps the last pose (used for rest).",
    "'derive' builds a gait from another one: 'negate' flips the sign of listed joints,",
    "'mirror' swaps left/right joints and flips ANKLE and HEAD."
  ],
